  "description": "Tree location - rear garden&nbsp;Access - side access&nbsp;T1 - Approx. H12 S6 40DBH Ash impacting on boundry wall and bin store&nbsp;Fell as close as possible to ground level&nbsp;Apply appropriate herbicide&nbsp;T2 - Approx. H12 S6 40DBH Ash impacting on boundry wall and bin store&nbsp;Fell as close as possible to ground level&nbsp;Apply appropriate herbicide&nbsp;In order to ensure there is no long term loss of amenity value as required by S.197 of the Town and Country Planning Act (1990) and to adhere to the Hackney Local Plan 2033 policy LP51 B, a replacement tree will be planted in the vicinity of the front garden.&nbsp; The new tree will be Standard size (8-10 cm) girth, 3.0–3.5m height, a native species or one known to provide benefits to local wildlife, climate resilient, and a species which is not considered invasive in Hackney.&nbsp; The replacement tree shall be planted during the planting season at the time of felling (end October - end March) or during the next immediately available planting season.GRP1 - rear garden Bramble and mixed vegetation&nbsp;On survey date due to the high level of bramble and mixed vegetation it was not possible to access the far end of the garden.&nbsp;We advise at this stage to fell/strim all vegetation as close as possible to ground level and a return visit to survey the mature trees that may be in the rear.&nbsp;",
